{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02619",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 5.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.92,
      "end_seconds": 7.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Hi there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.74,
      "end_seconds": 15.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.9,
      "end_seconds": 22.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. Okay, where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 23.9,
      "end_seconds": 31.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "It's breathlessness building over weeks, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.39,
      "end_seconds": 35.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.48,
      "end_seconds": 44.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.85,
      "end_seconds": 52.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.37,
      "end_seconds": 55.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "It happens on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.9,
      "end_seconds": 60.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.68,
      "end_seconds": 67.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.28,
      "end_seconds": 74.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.95,
      "end_seconds": 76.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.86,
      "end_seconds": 81.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.71,
      "end_seconds": 92.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a dull ache on one side of the chest as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.74,
      "end_seconds": 99.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 99.74,
      "end_seconds": 106.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Mm, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.29,
      "end_seconds": 114.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.98,
      "end_seconds": 119.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.1,
      "end_seconds": 128.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "The dull ache on one side of the chest? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.93,
      "end_seconds": 133.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.94,
      "end_seconds": 137.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "I'd give it a seven, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.28,
      "end_seconds": 144.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Yes. Have you had breathlessness building over weeks before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.82,
      "end_seconds": 152.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "I, I had a similar thing about six months ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.66,
      "end_seconds": 160.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Have you noticed night sweats, coughing up blood, fever or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.51,
      "end_seconds": 178.29,
      "duration_seconds": 13.78,
      "text": "No, no night sweats, no coughing up blood, no fever. I did have a dry cough at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.18,
      "end_seconds": 183.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "So, how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.99,
      "end_seconds": 186.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "No, uh, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.68,
      "end_seconds": 189.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.54,
      "end_seconds": 191.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.86,
      "end_seconds": 195.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 197.43,
      "end_seconds": 202.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "I mean, it's metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.02,
      "end_seconds": 206.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Okay, how long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 207.34,
      "end_seconds": 220.21,
      "duration_seconds": 12.87,
      "text": "About two months. I mean, she takes glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast. It's ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.14,
      "end_seconds": 227.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "I, I had amlodipine at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.05,
      "end_seconds": 231.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.17,
      "end_seconds": 235.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Just my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.03,
      "end_seconds": 239.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.32,
      "end_seconds": 244.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.96,
      "end_seconds": 246.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.21,
      "end_seconds": 251.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.42,
      "end_seconds": 258.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.69,
      "end_seconds": 263.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.82,
      "end_seconds": 266.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.77,
      "end_seconds": 271.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.36,
      "end_seconds": 277.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.57,
      "end_seconds": 279.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 281.11,
      "end_seconds": 291.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "Actually, uh, I remember she had some kind of reaction to erythromycin before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.48,
      "end_seconds": 298.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.04,
      "end_seconds": 305.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.41,
      "end_seconds": 312.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "My sister had breast cancer. Let me think, my brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.91,
      "end_seconds": 316.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.25,
      "end_seconds": 338.58,
      "duration_seconds": 19.33,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure. Diabetes, for nearly five years. Yes, high blood pressure. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I've got gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.58,
      "end_seconds": 346.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Yes, heart failure and gout are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 360.53,
      "end_seconds": 372.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.81,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 22, blood pressure 136 over 72, oxygen saturation is 94 percent, temperature 37.4, pulse is 94 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.16,
      "end_seconds": 378.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.08,
      "end_seconds": 383.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.54,
      "end_seconds": 386.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.15,
      "end_seconds": 407.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "There is dullness to percussion and reduced breath sounds at the right base."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.07,
      "end_seconds": 429.61,
      "duration_seconds": 19.54,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. From what you've told me and what I found, this is probably a pleural effusion needing a cause. We shouldn't forget a tumour. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had breathlessness building over weeks, moderate, and no night sweats or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.67,
      "end_seconds": 432.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.4,
      "end_seconds": 443.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Any scans or blood work done already?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 444.53,
      "end_seconds": 453.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "I did have a CT scan of the chest done last month, but the paper's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.63,
      "end_seconds": 472.77,
      "duration_seconds": 18.14,
      "text": "Let's book a chest X-ray to look into breathlessness. Let's book a pleural fluid sample to look into pleural effusion. I am arranging an urgent chest clinic review. The chest clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 473.62,
      "end_seconds": 474.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 475.09,
      "end_seconds": 487.47,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. Let's review you after the scan. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 488.52,
      "end_seconds": 490.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}